---
import Legal from "../layouts/Legal.astro";
import { LEGAL_UPDATED } from "../data/legal";
---

<Legal
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="This site sets no cookies, runs no analytics, and tracks nobody. Here is exactly what happens when you visit, and the three third parties involved."
  updated={LEGAL_UPDATED}
  current="privacy"
>
  <div class="callout">
    <p>
      <strong>The short version.</strong> This website sets no cookies, runs no
      analytics, and has no advertising or tracking of any kind. We do not build
      a profile of you, and we have nothing to sell to anybody because we do not
      collect anything. What follows is the detail, including the three outside
      services a page can contact.
    </p>
  </div>

  <p>
    This policy covers <strong>honeybearkatherine.org</strong>. It is operated
    by Katherine L. Carter, referred to here as "we".
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect directly</h2>

  <p>
    <strong>Nothing, unless you send it to us.</strong> There are no accounts,
    no logins, no newsletter sign-up, and no forms that run in the background.
  </p>

  <p>
    If you email us or use the contact form, we receive what you chose to send:
    your name, your email address, and your message. We use it to reply to you
    and for nothing else. We do not add you to a mailing list, and we do not
    pass it on.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies and storage</h2>

  <p>
    <strong>This site sets no cookies.</strong> It does not use local storage,
    session storage, fingerprinting, pixels, beacons, or any similar technology.
    There is no cookie banner because there is nothing to consent to.
  </p>

  <p>
    Note that a video player, once you press play, may set cookies of its own.
    That is covered below.
  </p>

  <h2>Analytics</h2>

  <p>
    There are none. We do not use Google Analytics or any comparable service, so
    we cannot tell you how many people read a given article, and we are content
    with that trade.
  </p>

  <h2>The three outside services</h2>

  <p>
    A website cannot avoid every third party. These are the only ones this site
    contacts, and what each one receives.
  </p>

  <h3>Vercel — hosting</h3>
  <p>
    The site is hosted by Vercel Inc. Like any web host, their servers process
    your IP address and basic request information in order to deliver the page,
    and keep short-term operational logs for security and reliability. We do not
    have access to a per-visitor record of who read what.
  </p>

  <h3>Google Fonts — typefaces</h3>
  <p>
    Page text is set in typefaces loaded from Google's font service. Loading
    them transmits your IP address and browser details to Google. We do not
    receive that information. If this matters to you, most browsers and content
    blockers can block font requests, and the site remains readable without
    them.
  </p>

  <h3>YouTube — episodes</h3>
  <p>
    Episodes are hosted on YouTube. We embed them using YouTube's
    privacy-enhanced mode (<strong>youtube-nocookie.com</strong>), which does not
    set advertising cookies before you interact. Episode thumbnails are loaded
    from YouTube's image servers, which means YouTube receives your IP address
    when a page with thumbnails loads.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Once you press play, YouTube's own terms apply</strong> and Google
    may set cookies and collect data as described in{" "}
    <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's privacy policy</a>.
    That is between you and Google; we receive nothing from it.
  </p>

  <h3>If you use the contact form</h3>
  <p>
    Where a contact form is available, it is delivered by Web3Forms, which
    forwards your message to our email and does not require an account. Your
    message passes through their systems in transit. If you would rather avoid
    that, message Katherine directly on one of the social accounts listed
    on the <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Links that leave this site</h2>

  <p>
    When you follow a link to YouTube, Amazon, RYZE, Cash App, a
    crisis organisation, or anywhere else, you are on their site under their
    policy. Affiliate links may set their own cookies to attribute a purchase —
    see the <a href="/disclaimer">disclaimer</a> for which links those are.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>

  <p>
    Privacy laws including the California Consumer Privacy Act and the UK and EU
    GDPR give people rights to access, correct, delete, and port their personal
    information, and to object to its processing.
  </p>

  <p>
    Those rights are straightforward here: <strong>the only personal
    information we hold is correspondence you chose to send us.</strong> Ask us
    to delete it and we will, and confirm when it is done. We have no other
    records to produce.
  </p>

  <p>
    <strong>We have never sold or shared personal information</strong> for
    advertising or any other purpose, and we do not intend to. There is no "do
    not sell my information" mechanism on this site because there is nothing
    that would need one.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>

  <p>
    This site deals with adult relationships and is not directed at children
    under 13. We do not knowingly collect information from them. If you believe
    a child has sent us something, contact us and we will delete it.
  </p>

  <h2>Security and retention</h2>

  <p>
    Correspondence is kept only as long as it is useful for the conversation it
    belongs to, and then deleted. No system is perfectly secure, and email in
    particular should not be treated as confidential. If your situation is
    sensitive, please contact one of the organisations on the{" "}
    <a href="/resources">resources page</a> rather than emailing us — they are
    equipped for it and we are not.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>

  <p>
    If this policy changes, the date at the top of the page changes with it. If
    a change is significant, we will say so on the site rather than quietly
    editing.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>

  <p>
    Questions about privacy, or a request about your information, can go through <a href="/contact">the contact page</a>.
  </p>
</Legal>
